    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "268fa2ca-6944-38b0-b04d-d94d1ed9b745",
                "word": "guerdon",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "745a18a1-2590-429a-9805-140b6f4ad07c",
                        "entry_id": "268fa2ca-6944-38b0-b04d-d94d1ed9b745",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "guerdons"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                        "entry_id": "268fa2ca-6944-38b0-b04d-d94d1ed9b745",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A reward, prize or recompense for a service; an accolade."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e0149dd-cf8a-49f8-8d39-8a0297780f9b",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "For would she of her gentlenesse,\nWithouten more, me ones kesse,\nIt were to me a great guerdoon.\nRelease of all my passion […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4c1d77f-7d3a-4a43-b221-9cf2bff0f419",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "Is this the guerdon wherewithall ye quite my fruitfulnesse?\nIs this the honor that ye gave for my plenteousnesse\nAnd dutie done with true intent?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd34a405-1a2c-419b-98f6-b20ebc712b1b",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "Done to death by slanderous tongues\nWas the Hero that here lies:\nDeath, in guerdon of her wrongs,\nGives her fame which never dies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d1f0e62-5ecb-44ef-b6b2-7db5c60bf2cb",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "He hearkned, and did stay from further harmes,\nTo gayne so goodly guerdon, as she spake […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "599d9f65-965c-4295-978e-9b7af5697d83",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "Fame is the spur that the clear spirit doth raise\n(That last infirmity of noble mind)\nTo scorn delights and live laborious days;\nBut the fair guerdon when we hope to find,\nAnd think to burst out into sudden blaze,\nComes the blind Fury with th'abhorred shears,\nAnd slits the thin-spun life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d5b0c6a-4a12-49ec-aaee-eb841308fb0d",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "Verse, like the laurel its immortal meed,\nShould be the guerdon of a noble deed"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "999130e3-961f-4285-af3d-b80b4d4e69bb",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "\"That will I do blithely,\" replied the Pilgrim, \"and without guerdon; my oath, for a time, prohibits me from touching gold.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e34f14d4-de0e-4131-bd68-ffc4f8c9417b",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "I had some faint recollection of having a penny-piece in my waistcoat pocket, and, pleased with the service he had rendered to us, I gave it him as his guerdon. \"Thank ye, sir—thank ye, sir—thank ye, sir,\" he cried, and immediately returned to his station near the footway."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a88b04a-9b19-4464-a982-8a225c6df07b",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "\"Here, minstrel, drive bad thoughts away! Sing! Take\n\"My glove for guerdon!\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ccca96d-8785-4de6-8a1d-a3e8c33c4cf1",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "You treat me like a slave, and bid me bow to my master! Is this the guerdon of a free maiden—is this the price of a life’s passion?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56fd4973-9767-4169-9d1b-db537d3a02c8",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "Sons of honour, nobly fathered, scions of the sturdy brood,Who from age to age have gathered strength and duty in the blood,Strength to bear the distressed burden, duty which has cost them dear—Wounds for wage and death for guerdon—Lo! the final hour is here. […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7372a120-2d1a-44d5-85cb-6b67bd1405a1",
                                "sense_id": "4217debd-51bc-380e-b576-e208d2c8685d",
                                "text": "Melanie might have given him his new coat but this sash was her gift, her own secret guerdon for him to wear into battle, something that would make him remember her every time he looked at it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
